WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.951 --> 00:00:17.972
twenty-four," counted Aladdin.

2
00:00:19.473 --> 00:00:21.494
He felt for the next step with his foot.

3
00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:24.636
"Twenty-five." The stairway was dark.

4
00:00:24.656 --> 00:00:29.658
"I must be careful," he said softly to himself.

5
00:00:29.678 --> 00:00:35.282
"Thirty." Soon Aladdin saw something below in the darkness.

6
00:00:35.302 --> 00:00:39.845
"A light," he said as he slowly stepped down.

7
00:00:39.865 --> 00:00:43.647
"Forty-two." The light was getting brighter.

8
00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:46.409
"Forty-eight, forty-nine."

9
00:00:46.449 --> 00:00:47.670
He was almost there!

10
00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:53.674
"Fifty!" Aladdin slipped through a narrow doorway and looked around.

11
00:00:53.694 --> 00:00:55.715
"It's the golden chamber!"

12
00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:56.616
he cried.

13
00:00:58.632 --> 00:01:02.814
And there stood the four golden jars, just as Magrib had said.

14
00:01:02.834 --> 00:01:07.317
"Don't touch anything," Aladdin reminded himself.

15
00:01:08.437 --> 00:01:11.459
Just then a light wind tickled his face.

16
00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:13.240
"What's that?"

17
00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.261
he wondered.

18
00:01:15.401 --> 00:01:19.523
A stronger wind sent the end of his sash toward a golden jar.

19
00:01:19.543 --> 00:01:23.726
"Hey!" said Aladdin, pulling his sash back.

20
00:01:23.746 --> 00:01:27.848
"I wonder if there's a spirit in here," he whispered.

21
00:01:29.644 --> 00:01:31.706
Then Aladdin's cap blew off.

22
00:01:32.927 --> 00:01:36.109
"Stop!" he called to no one as he jumped to catch it.

23
00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:41.013
He slid across the floor and almost hit a golden jar.

24
00:01:41.974 --> 00:01:42.954
Aladdin gulped.

25
00:01:42.974 --> 00:01:44.436
"That was close!"

26
00:01:46.457 --> 00:01:50.000
Holding his cap, he ran to a large door just ahead of him.

27
00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:52.262
"My name is Aladdin!"

28
00:01:52.462 --> 00:01:53.102
he shouted.

29
00:01:53.122 --> 00:01:55.004
"I command you to open!"

30
00:01:55.872 --> 00:02:00.033
The door swung open, and Aladdin stepped into a beautiful garden.

31
00:02:01.113 --> 00:02:04.254
The air smelled like sweet flowers and ripe fruit.

32
00:02:06.075 --> 00:02:06.695
He looked up.

33
00:02:07.255 --> 00:02:08.756
"Oranges!" he said.

34
00:02:08.776 --> 00:02:10.116
"Lemons and limes!

35
00:02:10.536 --> 00:02:11.456
Pears and plums!"

36
00:02:12.537 --> 00:02:14.017
Aladdin was getting hungry.

37
00:02:14.817 --> 00:02:16.678
He wished he could eat one of the plums.

38
00:02:17.758 --> 00:02:19.058
Then his face lit up.

39
00:02:19.078 --> 00:02:24.460
"Uncle said I can pick all the fruit I want when I have the lamp," he thought.

40
00:02:26.016 --> 00:02:28.277
The garden path was right under his feet.

41
00:02:29.698 --> 00:02:35.962
"One, two, three," he said, counting his steps as he walked between the trees.

42
00:02:37.182 --> 00:02:41.165
Exactly one hundred steps later, Aladdin arrived at the ladder.

43
00:02:42.285 --> 00:02:42.866
He looked up.

44
00:02:43.446 --> 00:02:45.907
The top was hidden high in the treetops.

45
00:02:47.888 --> 00:02:49.669
Slowly, Aladdin climbed.

46
00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.952
When he got to the top, the hole in the wall was in shadow.

47
00:02:55.084 --> 00:02:57.706
But Aladdin could see the lamp hanging from a chain.

48
00:02:58.966 --> 00:03:02.368
He reached in, took it, and held it in his hands.

49
00:03:02.388 --> 00:03:08.211
"It's just a dirty, old brass lamp," he said, shaking his head.

50
00:03:08.231 --> 00:03:10.192
"I don't want to mess up my jacket."

51
00:03:11.293 --> 00:03:15.695
So Aladdin wrapped the lamp in his sash and tucked it in his back pocket.

52
00:03:16.756 --> 00:03:18.857
Then he climbed back down the ladder.

53
00:03:18.877 --> 00:03:23.540
"Now," he said, "I'll get something to eat."

54
00:03:24.724 --> 00:03:28.367
But when Aladdin stepped to the ground, he couldn't believe what he saw.

55
00:03:29.508 --> 00:03:32.070
The oranges, lemons, and limes were gone.

56
00:03:33.071 --> 00:03:34.893
The pears and plums were gone too.

57
00:03:36.814 --> 00:03:40.598
Instead, the fruit trees were covered with sparkling jewels.

58
00:03:40.618 --> 00:03:43.480
"The fruit has turned to glass!"

59
00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:44.521
said Aladdin.

60
00:03:45.682 --> 00:03:48.064
He picked a bright-red jewel off a tree.

61
00:03:48.084 --> 00:03:51.467
"I can't eat this," he said with a shrug.

62
00:03:51.487 --> 00:03:52.488
"But it's pretty.

63
00:03:52.896 --> 00:03:54.777
I'll pick the glass fruit and take it to Mother."

64
00:03:56.298 --> 00:03:59.360
Aladdin was young, and he had always been poor.

65
00:04:00.681 --> 00:04:05.664
He didn't know these were precious gems—emeralds, diamonds, and rubies.

66
00:04:06.865 --> 00:04:08.125
They weren't glass at all.

67
00:04:09.266 --> 00:04:14.389
He began stuffing the jewels into the pockets of his jacket and pants until they bulged.

68
00:04:14.409 --> 00:04:18.892
"Now, I must return to my uncle," he told himself.

69
00:04:20.048 --> 00:04:24.291
He hurried through the golden chamber and started up the steps toward Magrib.

70
00:04:25.612 --> 00:04:30.096
Aladdin's load was so heavy that he could barely climb the stone stairway.

71
00:04:31.957 --> 00:04:37.181
And when he had almost reached the top, he could not get up the last step, which was

72
00:04:37.261 --> 00:04:38.422
taller than the others.

73
00:04:38.442 --> 00:04:41.445
"Uncle," he called out.

74
00:04:41.465 --> 00:04:42.686
"I'm back!

75
00:04:42.706 --> 00:04:43.726
Help me!"
